cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Kymora: High-Throughput Batch and Streaming Time-Series Feature Extraction with a Native Rust Computational Core"
authors:
  - family-names: Kumar
    given-names: Aamod
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, Uttar Pradesh, India"
version: 0.7.0
date-released: 2026-10-04
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Aamodx6/Kymora"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/kymora/"
keywords:
  - time-series
  - feature-extraction
  - rust
  - pyo3
  - numpy
abstract: >-
  Kymora is a batch-oriented Python time-series feature extraction library
  with a Rust core: zero-copy NumPy buffer ingestion, GIL release across the
  parallel region, Rayon work-stealing across the series dimension, and a
  curated 33-feature low-redundancy catalog computed through fused
  single-traversal passes.
